            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A person or group who has strayed from God, fallen into sin, or become spiritually lost and vulnerable, requiring rescue, repentance, and restoration by the Good Shepherd.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Luke 15:3-7\",\"Matthew 18:12-14\",\"Isaiah 53:6\",\"Psalm 119:176\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Specifically the ethnic people of Israel who have strayed from their covenant with God and lack faithful spiritual leadership.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 10:6\",\"Matthew 15:24\",\"Jeremiah 50:6\",\"Matthew 9:36\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Backslidden Christians or church members who have wandered away from the fellowship of believers but are still sought by God.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 18:12-14\",\"James 5:19-20\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The marginalized, outcast, and socially vulnerable who are exploited or neglected by corrupt religious and political authorities.\",\"basis\":[\"Ezekiel 34:4-16\",\"Luke 15:1-2\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The lost sheep is one of the most universally recognized biblical metaphors, primarily drawn from Jesus parables in Luke 15 and Matthew 18, and deeply rooted in Old Testament prophetic imagery regarding Israel and humanity's propensity to wander.\"}",
